course: dictionary
lesson: 1630
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chick is a baby bird, especially a baby chicken that has just hatched from its egg. «Some rare birds lay a second egg if the first is taken, so a zoo can hatch two chicks instead of one.» Here the zoo hatches two baby birds, so chicks must be babies that come out of eggs.
explain: Read the words around a word to choose its meaning. «Chicks are covered in soft fluffy down.» Down is the soft fluffy covering on a baby bird, so the clues show that a chick is young, fluffy and just out of its egg.
explain: Chick has a second meaning too. It is old-fashioned slang for a young woman, and many people find it rude. Do not use it about people. When you read chick, check the sentence: if it talks about eggs, nests or hens, it means a baby bird.
fact: A chick is a baby bird, especially a baby chicken.
fact: A chicken egg takes about 21 days to hatch if it is kept warm, which is about three weeks.
fact: A chick uses a hard tip on its beak, called the egg tooth, to crack the shell.
fact: The life cycle goes: egg, chick, then adult hen or rooster.
fact: «Don't count your chickens before they hatch» means don't plan on something that has not happened yet.
exercise: «A chick hatched from the egg this morning.» What is a chick? | A grown-up hen that lays eggs | A nest made of twigs | An egg that never hatches | *A baby bird, especially a baby chicken
exercise: «Chicks are covered in soft fluffy down.» What is down? | A hard shell | Sharp claws | *Soft fluffy feathers | Dry grass for a nest
exercise: «Keep the egg warm, and after about three weeks the chick will hatch.» What does hatch mean? | To lay an egg | To fly away from a nest | To sit in a box | *To come out of an egg
test: «Wash your hands after touching chicks, because they can carry germs like salmonella.» Why should you wash your hands? | Chicks are dirty and smelly | Washing keeps the chicks warm | Chicks bite hard | *Chicks can carry germs
test: «A hen's egg must be kept warm for about three weeks before the chick hatches.» How long does it take? | About three hours | About three years | *About three weeks | About three days
exam: Put the life cycle in the right order. | *egg, chick, adult hen | chick, egg, adult hen | egg, adult hen, chick | adult hen, chick, egg
